---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 9, 2026';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy — GFR Calculator"
	description="Privacy policy for GFR Calculator: what data this eGFR calculator collects, how it is used, and how your calculator inputs stay in your browser."
>
	<article class="container-page py-14 sm:py-20">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
			<p class="font-mono text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-mute">Privacy Policy</p>
			<h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-faint">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

			<p class="mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				This Privacy Policy explains what information GFR Calculator ("we," "our," or "this site")
				collects when you use gfrcalc.com, and how that information is used. We designed this
				calculator to require no sign-up and no account, and to keep your health inputs on your
				own device.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Calculator inputs</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				The creatinine, age, sex, and weight values you enter into the GFR calculator are
				processed entirely in your browser using client-side JavaScript. These values are never
				transmitted to our servers, stored in a database, or shared with any third party. If you
				close the tab or refresh the page, your inputs and results are gone.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Analytics and usage data</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				We may use privacy-respecting analytics tools to understand aggregate traffic patterns,
				such as which pages are visited and which browsers or devices are used. This data is
				anonymized or aggregated where possible and is not used to identify you personally, and it
				is separate from any calculator input you type into the tool.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Cookies and local storage</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				This site uses your browser's local storage to remember a single preference: whether you
				have selected light or dark mode. No advertising or tracking cookies are set by this site.
				Third-party analytics scripts, if enabled, may set their own cookies as described in their
				respective privacy policies.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Third-party links</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				Our <a href="/methodology" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">methodology</a> page and
				footer link to external medical references and research sources. We are not responsible
				for the privacy practices of those third-party sites.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Children's privacy</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				This calculator is intended for use by adults aged 18 and over and is not directed at
				children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page
				with an updated "Last updated" date.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Contact us</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please visit our
				<a href="/contact" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">Contact Us</a> page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</Layout>
